{# ── ONE MESSAGE OF SUPPORT, RENDERED ONCE ────────────────────────────────────
   Used by the ballot's wall, by /vote/{prog}/{slug}/messages and by /m/{token}: one
   renderer, so a change to how somebody's words are shown — or to what the report button
   does — cannot land in one place and not the other (VoteMessageTest).

   Destroyed and rebuilt in Phase 5 without Alpine (the shell does not load it): the cheer
   and report controls are plain buttons that vote.js binds by delegation, POSTing to
   /api/vote-message/cheer|report. Without script they stay inert buttons — the words, the
   name and the link to the message's own page all render on the server.

   Context: m (a row from VoteMessageService::wall).

   `m.name` has ALREADY been resolved against the voter's consent by the service and arrives
   as "A supporter" where consent was not given. Nothing here has the real name in scope —
   a template that held it would be one edit away from printing it. #}
<li class="vmi" data-vmi="{{ m.token }}">
  <blockquote class="vmi__b">“{{ m.body }}”</blockquote>
  <footer class="vmi__f">
    <span class="vmi__who">
      <span class="vmi__n">{{ m.name }}</span>
      {% if m.source == 'paid' %}<span class="vmi__tag">{{ 'backed with votes'|trans }}</span>{% endif %}
    </span>
    {% if m.token %}
    <span class="vmi__acts">
      {# Open to anybody, a stranger from a WhatsApp link included: these messages are about
         named people, and the reader who notices something wrong is rarely a member. One
         tap, no form; the reply is the same whether this is the first report or the one
         that trips the threshold. #}
      <button type="button" class="vmi__act" data-vmi-cheer aria-pressed="false" data-on="{{ 'You cheered this'|trans }}">
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 9V5a3 3 0 0 0-3-3l-4 9v11h11.28a2 2 0 0 0 2-1.7l1.38-9a2 2 0 0 0-2-2.3ZM7 22H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3"/></svg>
        <span data-vmi-n>{{ m.cheers ?: 'Cheer'|trans }}</span>
      </button>
      <a class="vmi__act" href="/m/{{ m.token }}">{{ 'Share this'|trans }}</a>
      <button type="button" class="vmi__act vmi__act--report" data-vmi-report data-done="{{ 'Reported'|trans }}">{{ 'Report'|trans }}</button>
    </span>
    {% endif %}
  </footer>
</li>
